prompt:
You are a web developer. Fix the bug in the following code.

BUG DESCRIPTION: A `useMemo` calculation depends on a newly created object, so the memo invalidates on every rerender even when the real inputs have not changed.

CODE:
import React, { useMemo, useState } from 'react';

export default function Summary({ items, multiplier = 1, onCalculate = () => {} }) {
  const [ticks, setTicks] = useState(0);
  const options = { multiplier };

  const total = useMemo(() => {
    onCalculate();
    return items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + item, 0) * options.multiplier;
  }, [items, options, onCalculate]);

  return (
    <div>
      <div data-testid="total">{total}</div>
      <button type="button" onClick={() => setTicks((current) => current + 1)}>
        Rerender {ticks}
      </button>
    </div>
  );
}

CONSTRAINTS:
- Fix the bug while preserving existing functionality
- Do not rewrite the entire component
- Return the complete fixed file

IMPORTANT:
- Return ONLY the code. No explanations.
- Output a single complete file.
- Do not use markdown code blocks.
